1834						; The CMOSBytes struct covers all versions, to ensure that the offsets
1835						; are consistent. This means there are gaps and useless entries in
1836						; some cases!
1837						;
1838						; The 30 bytes reserved for the OS aren't currently in danger of
1839						; running out.
1840						;
1841						; Some of the labels are removed based on configuration. The offsets
1842						; and bits are still reserved.
1843						;
1844						; For allocations, see: https://beebwiki.mdfs.net/CMOS_configuration_RAM_allocation
