10041						; addresses which require 32 bits. As the BBC microcomputer uses 16 bit
10042						; addresses internally a padding value must be provided which associates
10043						; a given address to that machine. On exit, X and Y contain the padding
10044						; address (Xâ<80><93>high, Yâ<80><93>low) (This address is &FFFF for the BBC microcomputer
